cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Replication materials for: When Multi-Venue Benchmarks Become Effectively Concentrated: Evidence from Fragmented BTCUSD Markets"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Jin"
    given-names: "Junjie"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jjjfee/btc-reference-price-fragmentation"
abstract: >
  Code, selected outputs, validation reports, and source-data manifests for the
  paper “When Multi-Venue Benchmarks Become Effectively Concentrated: Evidence
  from Fragmented BTCUSD Markets.” The study examines effective concentration
  in fragmented cryptocurrency benchmarks by comparing VWAP with a
  Liquidity-Weighted Median Price (LWMP) computed from synchronized
  dollar-volume proxy weights under the lower weighted-median convention.
keywords:
  - BTCUSD
  - benchmark design
  - effective concentration
  - fragmented markets
  - VWAP
  - LWMP
  - liquidity-weighted median
  - weighted median
  - reference price
license: "MIT"
version: "0.3.0"
date-released: 2026-07-21
